# reelkit settings. All optional. `npm run doctor` shows what's in effect.
#
#   cp .env.example .env    (.env is gitignored; never commit a key)

# --- ElevenLabs: read from .env or the environment ---------------------------

# Narrate with ElevenLabs. The house voice still comes first where it's installed; set REELS_VOICE=elevenlabs to override.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Voice to use. Default: the account's first stock voice (Jessica, Laura, Sarah…). List them: node src/tts.mjs --voices
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
# Model to use. Default: the newest the account can use (v4, then v3, then multilingual v2).
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL=

# --- Everything else: read from the environment only -------------------------
# Export these in your shell or set them per command, e.g.
#   REELS_VOICE=kokoro npm run reel -- --url https://…

# Narrator: qwen-locked (house voice), elevenlabs, kokoro or say (macOS). Default: house voice, else ElevenLabs with a key, else Kokoro.
# REELS_VOICE=
# Claude model that writes the script (passed to claude --model).
# REELS_MODEL=opus
# Brand pack: a folder in brands/ or a path to one.
# REELKIT_BRAND=creators-toolbox
# A Creators Toolbox checkout to read the catalog from live, instead of catalog/tools.json.
# REELKIT_SITE=/path/to/Creators-Toolbox
# Look: paper (cut paper) or studio (the site's clean design system).
# REELS_THEME=paper
# Set to 0 to render the studio look flat, without the paper texture.
# REELS_TEXTURE=1
# Hook title style: strips, letters, print or sign. An episode's own titleStyle wins.
# REELS_HOOK=strips
# Most media items (images, clips) collected per reel.
# REELS_MEDIA_MAX=12
# Set to 0 to skip Whisper word alignment; captions and lip sync then use estimated timing.
# REELS_ALIGN=1
# Date (YYYY-MM-DD, UTC) to treat as today when picking news.
# REELS_TODAY=
# How long the script writer may run, in milliseconds (15 minutes).
# REELS_WRITER_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
# The claude CLI to run.
# CLAUDE_CLI=claude
# Chrome or Chromium for page captures. Default: Google Chrome.app on macOS; on Linux, set it.
# CHROME_PATH=/usr/bin/google-chrome
# Port for the local viewer (npm run serve).
# PORT=4310
